    {
      "id": 145737,
      "name": "Darrell",
      "username": "Darrell",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/darrell/{size}/4836_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-06T18:59:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dshields\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dshields/48/1968_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dshields:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Well I rewatched the Video, and I still think I should have got my home run at my first at bat, it was a Strike 6, but I had a +1 power so I rolled a 6+1=7 Hit, but becuase I Rolled a Natural 6, I should still have gotten my smash, and I comfirmed it with another 6 for a Home run.&nbsp;&nbsp;But it was alot of fun, and I am still proud to be a World Champ.I am hopeing to Defend my title next Gen-Con.&nbsp;Thanks for a great game guys I can’t wait to get my Kickstarter!!!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Denis</p>\n<p>Here’s the deal with that- Mike and Chris are wrong. You can not Crush off a tied S6 roll with a natural 6. That would be a foul (being tied strikes are fouls). Now, rodney can roll up to a 7, which you did and that is why there was the run phase. Rodney’s currently the only batter who can make Contact on a Strike 6 (because of that modifier). Now, if the pitcher rolled a S5, then yes- you would’ve totally Crushed it and then also hit the HomeRun.</p>\n<p>Hope that clears it up. I know the game was a lot to take in with learning the game and jumping right into the tourney. Next year we are making it a requirment to have to know the game to play. Still we had a blast and hope, ultimatly, you did as well. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:33.110Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 13373,
      "topic_slug": "bottom-of-the-9th-world-series",
      "display_username": "Darrell",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"dshields\"]\n\nWell I rewatched the Video, and I still think I should have got my home run at my first at bat, it was a Strike 6, but I had a +1 power so I rolled a 6+1=7 Hit, but becuase I Rolled a Natural 6, I should still have gotten my smash, and I comfirmed it with another 6 for a Home run.&nbsp;&nbsp;But it was alot of fun, and I am still proud to be a World Champ.I am hopeing to Defend my title next Gen-Con.&nbsp;Thanks for a great game guys I can't wait to get my Kickstarter!!!!\n\n[/quote]\n\nDenis\n\nHere's the deal with that- Mike and Chris are wrong. You can not Crush off a tied S6 roll with a natural 6. That would be a foul (being tied strikes are fouls). Now, rodney can roll up to a 7, which you did and that is why there was the run phase. Rodney's currently the only batter who can make Contact on a Strike 6 (because of that modifier). Now, if the pitcher rolled a S5, then yes- you would've totally Crushed it and then also hit the HomeRun.\n\nHope that clears it up. I know the game was a lot to take in with learning the game and jumping right into the tourney. Next year we are making it a requirment to have to know the game to play. Still we had a blast and hope, ultimatly, you did as well. :)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n",
